    {
      "id": "finding:sus:r4:3.1",
      "label": "Finding 3.1\nopenSUSE Leap 15.6 has severa…",
      "type": "Finding",
      "color": "#06D6A0",
      "status": null,
      "title": "openSUSE Leap 15.6 has several privilege escalation vulnerabilities that could allow local attackers to gain full root access. Sudo vulnerabilities (CVE-2025-32462, CVE-2025-32463) are present in the sudo package, which can be exploited via the `--host` and `chroot` options. Chained privilege escalation vulnerabilities (CVE-2025-6018, CVE-2025-6019) can be exploited to gain full root access. CVE-2025-6018 is a PAM misconfiguration, and CVE-2025-6019 is a vulnerability in `libblockdev` exploitable via the `udisks` daemon. Linux Kernel vulnerabilities (CVE-2024-50302, CVE-2017-1000253, CVE-2024-53104) can lead to privilege escalation.",
      "size": 32,
      "shape": "dot",
      "borderColor": "#212529",
      "borderWidth": 2,
      "font": {
        "color": "#212529"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "state:sus:r4:3.2",
      "label": "State 3.2\nSecurity Recommendations",
      "type": "State",
      "color": "#0B3D91",
      "status": "completed",
      "title": "3.2 Security Recommendations [completed]\nSecurity recommendations include: keeping systems updated, working with least privilege, monitoring security advisories, hardening system configuration, and hardening Polkit rules. For CVE-2025-6018 and CVE-2025-6019, mitigation involves applying security updates and hardening Polkit rules by changing the `org.freedesktop.udisks2.modify-device` policy from `allow_active=yes` to `auth_admin`.",
      "size": 40,
      "shape": "dot",
      "borderColor": "#212529",
      "borderWidth": 2,
      "font": {
